      "sourceContent": "The corporation operates in jurisdictions whose privacy and data-protection regimes — Canadian PIPEDA and Québec’s Law 25, European Union GDPR, California’s CCPA / CPRA, and various sectoral regulations — impose specific obligations on how personal data is collected, stored, processed, transferred, retained, and deleted. This chapter governs how cloud architecture supports compliance with those obligations. The objective is to ensure that every system processing personal data classifies its data correctly, places it in a region permitted by residency rules, encrypts it appropriately (Chapter 4), retains it only as long as necessary, supports data-subject rights, and produces audit evidence sufficient to satisfy regulators.",
